WEBVTT

00:01.087 --> 00:03.927
♪

00:05.807 --> 00:07.637
My math says we're on track.

00:07.727 --> 00:08.937
We should reach our target

00:09.017 --> 00:11.687
in about three minutes,
40 seconds from now.

00:11.767 --> 00:12.897
And once we get there,

00:13.227 --> 00:15.477
we'll have to deal
with the assassin and her agent?

00:15.897 --> 00:16.817
[gasps softly]

00:17.647 --> 00:19.987
Hey, where'd that musket
you were carrying go?

00:20.447 --> 00:22.987
I had to give it
to an acquaintance of mine.

00:23.697 --> 00:25.237
It looked like
they really wanted it,

00:25.327 --> 00:26.907
and I figured I might as well.

00:27.367 --> 00:28.867
You should be more careful
with it.

00:28.957 --> 00:31.997
That musket actually belonged
to Siesta, you know.

00:32.577 --> 00:34.377
Hold on, do you even have a plan

00:34.457 --> 00:36.247
for how we beat them
without a gun?

00:36.337 --> 00:38.587
Uh?
I guess I didn't get that far.

00:38.667 --> 00:39.717
You're kidding me.

00:40.257 --> 00:41.217
But...

00:42.087 --> 00:45.467
I'm willing to bet you have
some sort of plan, don't you?

00:47.137 --> 00:48.097
[exhales softly]

00:50.597 --> 00:53.227
[NOCHES] Oh, I see.
You're not going to tell me.

00:54.517 --> 00:55.977
-There they are.
-[gasps]

00:58.107 --> 00:59.487
[NOCHES] It's time to go.

01:12.577 --> 01:14.037
Kimizuka?

01:14.587 --> 01:18.257
What's that? Is that robot
seriously still functional?

01:19.877 --> 01:21.797
-Do it.
-Hm.

01:22.677 --> 01:23.637
[Noches gasps softly]

01:26.137 --> 01:27.507
[Kimizuka yelping]

01:28.507 --> 01:30.057
Guess they want to fight.

01:30.517 --> 01:32.887
Initiating punishment now.

01:35.607 --> 01:36.727
[Char gasps]

01:40.027 --> 01:41.947
Geez, you think you got 'em?

01:42.027 --> 01:44.657
The Sirius Version Beta
has serious strength.

01:44.737 --> 01:46.117
Yes, pun intended.

01:46.197 --> 01:47.827
Listen,
I know they got you once,

01:47.907 --> 01:50.407
but that's a brutal way
to get revenge, you know?

01:51.447 --> 01:52.327
[both gasp]

01:52.407 --> 01:54.077
[Char panting]

01:58.497 --> 01:59.417
[Char grunts]

02:01.797 --> 02:03.927
-[gasps]
-[NOCHES] I'll handle her.

02:04.007 --> 02:06.137
You just need to stay back,
Kimihiko.

02:06.547 --> 02:08.507
[grunting]

02:08.597 --> 02:11.597
[CHAR] Between you
and that damned vampire,

02:11.677 --> 02:14.347
none of this was ever
in the plan.

02:14.437 --> 02:15.897
That's your problem then.

02:15.977 --> 02:17.557
I wouldn't say
that's the right way

02:17.647 --> 02:18.817
to approach any of this.

02:18.897 --> 02:21.647
What? Are you really
lecturing me now?

02:21.727 --> 02:22.987
I'm not.

02:23.067 --> 02:25.357
I know it's not my place
to say so.

02:25.447 --> 02:28.867
But Siesta would have called
every single failure her own.

02:28.947 --> 02:30.077
She'd never blame others

02:30.157 --> 02:32.197
if the plan she made
went wrong in the end.

02:32.287 --> 02:33.247
[gasps]

02:34.037 --> 02:35.457
[gasps]

02:36.207 --> 02:38.247
Getting overly emotional
is a bad habit.

02:38.327 --> 02:40.337
You should think
about getting some therapy.

02:40.417 --> 02:41.627
[Char grunts]

02:43.837 --> 02:45.417
[CHAR] Ma'am was the same way.

02:45.507 --> 02:46.637
[Noches gasps softly]

02:46.927 --> 02:48.467
Well, it's been
a full five years

02:48.547 --> 02:50.007
since I first met her.

02:50.677 --> 02:52.767
A certain organization
we both know

02:52.847 --> 02:55.557
gave me clear orders to kill her
no matter what.

02:56.097 --> 02:57.557
♪

02:57.647 --> 03:00.107
[Char crying]

03:03.937 --> 03:05.107
[blows nose]

03:05.817 --> 03:07.157
Oh, go on, then.

03:07.237 --> 03:08.947
I blew my chance
to assassinate you,

03:09.027 --> 03:10.157
so just make it quick.

03:11.237 --> 03:13.367
They're going to kill me
for failing anyway,

03:13.447 --> 03:15.497
so you might as well
do it first.

03:15.577 --> 03:17.867
I told you how to handle this.

03:17.957 --> 03:20.377
Tell them I never
made it out of here alive.

03:20.457 --> 03:23.377
Then they shouldn't continue
looking for you anymore.

03:24.757 --> 03:26.167
I don't understand.

03:26.257 --> 03:28.137
How does that benefit you
in any way?

03:31.887 --> 03:34.137
Why are you even doing
a job like this?

03:34.217 --> 03:35.427
[CHAR] Mm...

03:36.227 --> 03:38.187
I'm inspired by my parents.

03:38.887 --> 03:40.437
They were soldiers and spies

03:40.517 --> 03:42.607
who fought for us
in the shadows.

03:43.357 --> 03:44.727
They kept this world safe,

03:44.817 --> 03:47.197
facing dangers
most of us never saw.

03:47.647 --> 03:49.157
So, I'm proud of their service,

03:49.947 --> 03:52.237
and I'm honored
to continue their mission.

03:53.197 --> 03:56.157
I see. I can understand that.

03:57.117 --> 03:58.287
Just like you,

03:58.367 --> 04:00.457
I have my own reasons
for doing this job.

04:01.327 --> 04:02.537
So, no matter what,

04:02.627 --> 04:04.627
I can't just let you
kill me here.

04:04.707 --> 04:05.917
[Char sighs]

04:06.297 --> 04:09.427
But of course,
if you're the same as me,

04:09.507 --> 04:11.177
you can't exactly
die here either.

04:11.257 --> 04:13.347
So, are you saying
you'll help me?

04:13.427 --> 04:14.467
Yes.

04:14.557 --> 04:16.137
After all this is over,

04:16.217 --> 04:18.767
I want you to help me through
whatever comes next.

04:18.847 --> 04:19.807
Huh?

04:20.437 --> 04:22.397
[SIESTA]
That's the deal I'm offering.

04:23.477 --> 04:26.227
I'll get you
out of here alive this time,

04:26.317 --> 04:27.897
and in exchange,

04:27.987 --> 04:31.107
you can help me once in a while,
when I really need you most.

04:31.907 --> 04:35.237
Uh... I tried to take your life,
you know?

04:35.327 --> 04:38.037
And now you're asking me
to help you get through this?

04:38.827 --> 04:40.037
How about it?

04:40.117 --> 04:41.417
Huh?

04:41.827 --> 04:44.537
[CHAR] I knew it deep down
before I could think it through.

04:45.417 --> 04:47.547
She didn't really need
my assistance at all,

04:47.627 --> 04:49.417
not even for a moment.

04:49.837 --> 04:51.717
She made it seem like
she needed me,

04:51.797 --> 04:54.137
so I'd just
let her help me instead,

04:54.217 --> 04:56.597
and that was her plan all along.

04:57.967 --> 04:59.427
No fair.

04:59.847 --> 05:00.937
[chuckles]

05:03.017 --> 05:04.857
[CHAR] So what should I do now?

05:04.937 --> 05:07.357
I mean,
what can I even do to help?

05:12.947 --> 05:14.697
And look at that,

05:14.777 --> 05:18.367
she gave me this pendant
as proof of our exclusive deal.

05:18.947 --> 05:22.407
She was the one who always
watched over me wherever I went.

05:22.497 --> 05:24.127
As long as I helped the Tuners,

05:24.207 --> 05:26.337
that organization
couldn't hurt me.

05:26.997 --> 05:29.047
She even had it all arranged,

05:29.127 --> 05:30.417
so that after she died,

05:30.507 --> 05:33.257
I could go work
for another Tuner immediately.

05:33.887 --> 05:36.097
And that person was Fuubi Kase?

05:36.717 --> 05:40.677
And even now, even in that form,
she could strike me down.

05:40.767 --> 05:45.107
She's still going easy on me,
so she won't end up killing me.

05:45.187 --> 05:46.647
Just tell me why?

05:47.187 --> 05:49.107
Why do you go so easy on me?

05:49.187 --> 05:51.147
Why don't you take me seriously?

05:51.237 --> 05:52.567
Because I don't get it.

05:52.647 --> 05:54.947
Why protect me
after all this time?

05:55.697 --> 05:58.407
A year ago,
I couldn't accomplish anything.

05:58.487 --> 06:01.617
That's when I swore,
whatever might happen to me

06:01.697 --> 06:03.827
while I was working
for that woman,

06:03.907 --> 06:05.917
I'd take on
every last member of SPES

06:05.997 --> 06:09.127
and defeat them all
in her place, no matter what.

06:09.207 --> 06:11.297
[inhales deeply] But you...

06:15.467 --> 06:16.387
[Noches sighs]

06:17.137 --> 06:18.257
[grunts]

06:18.847 --> 06:20.557
[CHAR] At any cost...

06:21.137 --> 06:23.437
-I'll do anything I can to win.
-[gasps]

06:26.807 --> 06:27.937
[CHAR] Right on cue.

06:28.017 --> 06:29.977
I knew you would do that.

06:30.067 --> 06:32.187
-It's over now.
-[grunts]

06:32.277 --> 06:34.197
-[KIMIZUKA] No, wait, Char.
-[Char gasps]

06:34.277 --> 06:37.487
Come on, could you really
pull that trigger?

06:37.567 --> 06:39.237
Are you saying I won't?

06:39.327 --> 06:41.537
You think I'd really hesitate
to do it now?

06:41.617 --> 06:45.327
You sure? Even if that's
the real Siesta's body?

06:45.407 --> 06:46.457
[Char gasps softly]

06:46.747 --> 06:47.827
Huh?

06:48.577 --> 06:51.627
Is that really you... ma'am?

06:53.757 --> 06:55.377
I didn't think you knew.

06:56.177 --> 06:59.177
So you want to tell me when
you figured it out, Kimihiko?

06:59.257 --> 07:01.307
I'm not exactly sure.

07:02.097 --> 07:04.557
You know, I don't think
it was any one thing

07:04.637 --> 07:06.017
that tipped me off.

07:07.897 --> 07:09.807
[NOCHES]
The battle was a year ago.

07:09.897 --> 07:11.687
They preserved Siesta's body...

07:12.187 --> 07:14.567
and fitted her
with a new artificial heart.

07:15.777 --> 07:17.737
Then came
an artificial intelligence

07:17.817 --> 07:20.407
programmed to remember
every moment of her life.

07:20.487 --> 07:24.327
And so, I was made from
her body, heart, and memories...

07:24.407 --> 07:26.367
and that is how I came to be.

07:26.457 --> 07:27.497
♪

07:28.247 --> 07:29.497
I had a hunch.

07:29.577 --> 07:32.627
It seemed like
the most likely case, after all.

07:32.707 --> 07:34.587
I recall how she smelled,

07:34.667 --> 07:37.087
even though
so much time has passed.

07:37.757 --> 07:39.677
But so what?
Even if that's her...

07:40.427 --> 07:43.177
that won't change the work
I'm here to do.

07:43.257 --> 07:46.097
And I'll do what I came here
to do regardless.

07:46.767 --> 07:47.887
[KIMIZUKA] Char, wait!

07:47.977 --> 07:51.357
What Siesta left behind
was the four of us.

07:51.437 --> 07:53.817
If you're gonna carry on
with your duty now,

07:53.897 --> 07:56.487
then all four of us
have to survive this.

07:57.237 --> 07:59.697
But she was a Tuner
who had one mission.

07:59.777 --> 08:02.867
Her duty was to defeat SPES
once and for all!

08:03.277 --> 08:04.327
It's true!

08:04.947 --> 08:07.157
But the teacher that you loved,
would she have chosen her duty,

08:07.247 --> 08:09.417
or the comrades
that have stood behind her

08:09.497 --> 08:11.037
-this whole time?
-[gun cocks]

08:11.127 --> 08:13.167
Shut up. [exclaims]

08:13.247 --> 08:14.547
♪

08:15.797 --> 08:16.917
[gasps softly]

08:21.007 --> 08:22.427
[grunts]

08:22.887 --> 08:24.217
It's wrong.

08:24.307 --> 08:25.597
Why is she smiling

08:25.677 --> 08:28.387
like she never had a care
in this world?

08:28.477 --> 08:29.437
It's this.

08:29.517 --> 08:31.307
-[gasps softly]
-This thing!

08:31.397 --> 08:32.267
[stomps]

08:32.357 --> 08:33.397
[Char gasps]

08:39.857 --> 08:40.777
♪

08:40.857 --> 08:42.027
Well, that hurt.

08:42.117 --> 08:45.277
[gasps] Oh, I'm so sorry.

08:52.577 --> 08:53.787
But why?

08:54.497 --> 08:56.337
-[NOCHES] Good grief.
-[gasps softly]

08:56.957 --> 08:59.587
You're stupid. I knew it.

09:01.927 --> 09:03.217
What'd you say?

09:06.217 --> 09:09.017
You know,
that's the first time...

09:09.427 --> 09:10.727
[sniffles]

09:10.807 --> 09:14.307
...for real,
you've ever said that to me.

09:14.397 --> 09:15.687
[gasps softly]

09:16.687 --> 09:17.857
[chuckles]

09:19.397 --> 09:20.937
-Ma'am.
-[gun cocks]

09:21.027 --> 09:21.987
[gun fires]

09:23.487 --> 09:24.487
[gasps softly]

09:24.567 --> 09:25.577
[gasps]

09:26.487 --> 09:27.657
[KIMIZUKA] Noches!

09:29.037 --> 09:30.037
♪

09:30.117 --> 09:31.457
[Noches breathes shakily]

09:31.537 --> 09:32.787
[CHAR] Ma'am!

09:34.327 --> 09:35.957
[FUUBI] There you have it.

09:36.037 --> 09:39.757
And that's exactly why
I called you naive, Charlotte.

09:39.837 --> 09:41.967
I imagined that
you were smarter than this,

09:42.047 --> 09:43.127
but alas...

09:43.757 --> 09:46.137
it seems you're no different
than that confused kid.

09:46.217 --> 09:47.257
[grunts]

09:47.347 --> 09:48.677
[KIMIZUKA] Noches!

09:48.757 --> 09:50.727
-[NOCHES] I'm fine.
-[gasps]

09:50.807 --> 09:52.977
Damage is assessed as minor.

09:53.057 --> 09:56.227
I can correct it by activating
emergency shutdown.

09:56.307 --> 09:58.727
-Sure, but...
-It's okay.

09:58.817 --> 10:01.897
Your top priority
is to handle her right now.

10:01.987 --> 10:03.237
Go after her!

10:06.737 --> 10:07.737
[NOCHES] Uh?

10:07.827 --> 10:09.987
I'll be back in just a moment.

10:10.077 --> 10:11.287
♪

10:11.697 --> 10:12.707
[chuckles softly]

10:17.627 --> 10:18.627
[FUUBI] Hm.

10:18.997 --> 10:19.997
What gives?

10:20.087 --> 10:22.257
You were just pretending
to be enemies,

10:22.337 --> 10:24.047
and now you're working together?

10:24.797 --> 10:26.847
You're really set
on fighting her?

10:26.927 --> 10:29.297
Are you sure you're ready
for what comes next?

10:29.387 --> 10:31.807
-You'll lose a lot, you know?
-Hmm.

10:31.887 --> 10:33.057
[Noches breathes softly]

10:34.887 --> 10:36.267
Too late to care.

10:37.727 --> 10:39.517
First attack from both sides.
[grunts]

10:42.357 --> 10:43.487
Too slow.

10:44.397 --> 10:45.697
[gasps]

10:47.027 --> 10:48.777
[grunting]

10:50.487 --> 10:51.907
All right, one down.

10:53.327 --> 10:54.827
[yelling]

10:54.907 --> 10:55.997
[both grunting]

10:56.077 --> 10:57.077
[Char gasps]

10:57.377 --> 10:58.877
[grunts]

11:02.507 --> 11:05.627
What'll you do?
You're the only one left now.

11:06.377 --> 11:09.467
Are you going to keep resisting
for no reason?

11:09.547 --> 11:11.887
Don't you care
what happens to the world?

11:12.677 --> 11:14.807
Of course I care
about what happens.

11:15.477 --> 11:18.687
She'd never want me to make
one person pay with their life

11:18.767 --> 11:20.647
just to keep
the entire world alive.

11:20.727 --> 11:23.107
She'd want me to find
another way to save them.

11:23.187 --> 11:24.687
[FUUBI] Think so?

11:24.777 --> 11:27.277
The one they actually sacrificed
to save the world

11:27.357 --> 11:28.697
said it herself.

11:28.777 --> 11:30.657
You were supposed to be
the last thing

11:30.737 --> 11:32.697
she could leave behind
for all of us.

11:32.777 --> 11:34.787
Do you know what that means?

11:36.537 --> 11:39.877
Simply put, you must become
the Great Detective

11:39.957 --> 11:42.707
and die to ensure the safety
of the entire world.

11:42.787 --> 11:44.257
[gasps softly]

11:44.337 --> 11:46.007
[FUUBI] I'll be honest with you.

11:46.547 --> 11:48.757
Nagisa Natsunagi is too weak.

11:48.837 --> 11:50.507
She can't win this on her own.

11:51.137 --> 11:54.767
So then, Charlotte,
you must honor her will

11:54.847 --> 11:57.727
and now rise
as the Great Detective, a Tuner.

11:58.137 --> 12:00.307
Didn't you always
look up to her?

12:02.767 --> 12:04.397
-You know...
-Hm?

12:05.397 --> 12:07.487
...while I did admire
the Great Detective,

12:07.567 --> 12:09.737
she wasn't the only one
I looked up to.

12:09.817 --> 12:11.657
The truth is...

12:13.077 --> 12:16.247
I looked up to the strong,
beautiful girl named Siesta

12:16.327 --> 12:18.287
more than
I ever did anyone else!

12:19.667 --> 12:21.287
How very boring.

12:22.877 --> 12:24.537
[both grunting]

12:26.967 --> 12:28.797
You underestimate me.

12:29.507 --> 12:30.757
[coughs]

12:30.837 --> 12:33.297
[groaning]

12:36.137 --> 12:37.307
-[gun cocks]
-[gasps]

12:38.097 --> 12:41.057
Did you really think
you could beat me one-on-one?

12:41.137 --> 12:42.307
[grunts]

12:43.517 --> 12:45.727
Playtime's over now, kid.

12:47.437 --> 12:48.317
Fire!

12:50.397 --> 12:51.317
[gasps]

12:53.907 --> 12:56.577
Nice hit, Nagisa! Like a pro!

12:56.657 --> 12:58.957
Siesta's seven tools
are amazing.

12:59.037 --> 13:00.957
There was no recoil at all.

13:01.537 --> 13:02.537
[scoffs]

13:03.127 --> 13:05.457
She really decided to come
all the way back here herself?

13:06.087 --> 13:07.047
But why?

13:07.587 --> 13:10.757
Seriously? You're still going
to take her side?

13:10.837 --> 13:12.137
Don't tell me you've forgotten

13:12.217 --> 13:14.297
that she's the one
who tried to kill you!

13:14.387 --> 13:15.467
[Char exhales softly]

13:15.887 --> 13:17.677
[SAIKAWA] Yes!
She's our comrade,

13:17.757 --> 13:18.767
no matter what!

13:18.847 --> 13:20.017
And after this,

13:20.097 --> 13:22.137
we're gonna have
one hell of a fight.

13:22.937 --> 13:25.607
You don't have a problem
with that, do you, Char?

13:25.687 --> 13:28.027
And she's not the only one,
either, you know.

13:28.107 --> 13:30.237
Yui and I are totally gonna
kill you twice.

13:30.317 --> 13:32.197
We're all in this together!

13:32.947 --> 13:35.277
Yui, Nagisa.

13:35.367 --> 13:38.327
[FUUBI] Don't worry, that's not
how this is going to end.

13:38.407 --> 13:39.287
[gasps]

13:39.827 --> 13:43.327
You're prepared to die now,
are you, Yui Saikawa?

13:43.917 --> 13:46.377
And you, Nagisa Natsunagi?

13:46.917 --> 13:48.377
[NATSUNAGI] Of course.

13:48.457 --> 13:51.757
Sorry, but I'm not gonna fire
any warning shots this time.

13:58.847 --> 13:59.767
[gasps]

13:59.847 --> 14:01.267
-Right there!
-Huh?

14:01.347 --> 14:03.137
[Fuubi pants]

14:05.557 --> 14:07.517
I knew I'd have
to take you out first.

14:09.977 --> 14:11.147
[grunts]

14:11.987 --> 14:13.277
[both scream]

14:13.357 --> 14:14.397
[Fuubi grunts]

14:17.527 --> 14:18.487
[gasps]

14:18.577 --> 14:19.657
[gunshot]

14:22.247 --> 14:23.537
[Fuubi groans]

14:30.207 --> 14:32.417
[both screaming]

14:36.547 --> 14:38.257
Yui! Nagisa!

14:38.347 --> 14:40.387
[panting]

14:43.517 --> 14:45.187
[grunting]

14:47.057 --> 14:48.187
Huh?

14:52.687 --> 14:53.647
[chuckles softly]

14:56.607 --> 14:58.367
[FUUBI] The three of you
are still pretending

14:58.447 --> 14:59.697
to be friends?

15:00.277 --> 15:01.867
How dumb are you?

15:01.947 --> 15:02.907
[Char grunts]

15:03.247 --> 15:05.037
That doesn't make us stupid!

15:05.497 --> 15:06.997
We're the ones
who carry the last hope

15:07.077 --> 15:08.707
that Siesta left behind.

15:09.127 --> 15:10.377
None of us will lose.

15:10.457 --> 15:12.377
-None of us will give up.
-[CHAR] Hm.

15:12.457 --> 15:14.297
We'll all win together!

15:16.007 --> 15:18.137
What is the deal
with you people?

15:18.217 --> 15:23.767
Comrades, bonds, friendship,
feelings, will.

15:23.847 --> 15:26.637
What good are all those things
to the real world?

15:26.727 --> 15:29.017
Yui Saikawa, if you die,

15:29.107 --> 15:31.107
everyone in the world
will be saved.

15:31.187 --> 15:33.437
Charlotte Arisaka Anderson,

15:33.527 --> 15:35.607
all you have to do
is kill Yui Saikawa,

15:35.687 --> 15:37.487
and the world will be saved.

15:37.567 --> 15:39.487
Natsunagi Nagisa,

15:39.567 --> 15:42.327
if you could be as strong
as the last Great Detective,

15:42.407 --> 15:44.497
the world would be saved!

15:45.077 --> 15:47.287
Why don't you just do it then?

15:47.367 --> 15:50.077
You can't, huh? I get it now.

15:50.167 --> 15:51.377
You're too weak.

15:52.037 --> 15:53.337
In that case,

15:53.417 --> 15:55.507
then you should at least
have the decency

15:55.587 --> 15:57.337
to be ashamed of that...

15:57.417 --> 15:59.757
and let the people who are
fighting to save the world

15:59.837 --> 16:01.137
do their jobs!

16:03.007 --> 16:04.137
You're not wrong.

16:04.217 --> 16:05.927
I don't think
there's anything wrong

16:06.017 --> 16:07.977
with the point
you're trying to make.

16:08.057 --> 16:09.387
Some people would even say

16:09.477 --> 16:11.057
what you're doing
is the right thing.

16:11.607 --> 16:15.277
But the detective
who was always right... is dead.

16:16.237 --> 16:17.437
And I'm here.

16:17.817 --> 16:19.907
I still wanna make that choice
for myself,

16:19.987 --> 16:22.027
even if it does turn out
that I'm wrong.

16:22.657 --> 16:23.987
I wanna choose a future

16:24.077 --> 16:25.537
where the people
I care about most

16:25.617 --> 16:28.037
are smiling with me
when it's all over and done.

16:28.117 --> 16:29.787
It's not black and white.

16:29.867 --> 16:32.537
We can win,
and no one has to die!

16:34.287 --> 16:36.207
What a waste of time.

16:37.377 --> 16:39.507
But at least that makes it easy.

16:40.177 --> 16:42.757
The last one still standing
at the end of all this

16:42.847 --> 16:43.927
is the winner.

16:44.007 --> 16:45.807
Evil Die.

16:49.477 --> 16:51.597
-Nagisa!
-[NATSUNAGI] Don't worry.

16:52.267 --> 16:55.067
I can't see her anywhere,
but I know she's there.

16:55.147 --> 16:56.897
She's looking at me even now.

16:57.357 --> 16:59.437
And she can hear
each word I say.

16:59.527 --> 17:00.857
So, there's no doubt in my mind

17:00.947 --> 17:02.487
that this power
is going to work.

17:03.817 --> 17:05.327
Fuubi Kase...

17:06.197 --> 17:07.447
You're frozen in place,

17:07.537 --> 17:09.077
and you can't even
move a muscle.

17:11.667 --> 17:13.327
[Fuubi grunting]

17:16.127 --> 17:18.757
So, you've got some
cheap new power to show off.

17:18.837 --> 17:21.627
Don't think for a second
it'll be enough to stop me.

17:23.137 --> 17:25.097
Wait a second.
You don't really think

17:25.177 --> 17:27.717
the three of you together
stand a chance against me?

17:27.807 --> 17:28.717
[gasps]

17:29.517 --> 17:30.597
Hold on.

17:32.267 --> 17:33.397
Three?

17:34.187 --> 17:36.067
That robot's out of commission.

17:36.647 --> 17:38.067
That can't be right.

17:38.437 --> 17:41.487
Since when have I been
up against all three of them?

17:42.277 --> 17:44.027
Hey, where did he go?

17:44.447 --> 17:46.827
Where is Kimihiko Kimizuka?

17:48.197 --> 17:49.157
[chuckles softly]

17:49.787 --> 17:51.247
[KIMIZUKA]
You made the right call,

17:51.327 --> 17:52.997
and I can understand why.

17:53.077 --> 17:54.747
Your priority was to focus

17:54.827 --> 17:57.417
on taking down Char
and the others.

17:58.297 --> 18:00.207
You could have handled
anything I tried

18:00.297 --> 18:01.837
and not broken a sweat.

18:02.837 --> 18:04.137
But even so,

18:04.217 --> 18:06.757
you made one mistake
that changes everything.

18:07.557 --> 18:10.217
[FUUBI]
Oh, no, Kimihiko Kimizuka.

18:11.347 --> 18:13.477
You ate Chameleon's seed!

18:14.597 --> 18:15.937
[chuckles]

18:16.017 --> 18:18.267
But side effects
kept cropping up.

18:18.357 --> 18:19.777
I don't give a shit.

18:20.937 --> 18:22.237
[KIMIZUKA] I'm pretty sure

18:22.317 --> 18:24.397
she'd give me hell
for doing this.

18:24.897 --> 18:26.907
But right now, all I care about

18:26.987 --> 18:29.737
is punching this
dipshit detective in the face.

18:29.827 --> 18:31.867
She's taken the justice
my partner loved

18:31.947 --> 18:33.497
and made a mockery of it.

18:33.577 --> 18:36.577
And all I want to do right now
is knock her damn lights out!

18:37.747 --> 18:39.587
Is that what
you really wanna do?

18:39.667 --> 18:40.667
[KIMIZUKA] Uh?

18:42.007 --> 18:43.127
[chuckles]

18:43.207 --> 18:45.797
Why not? I'm not causing trouble

18:45.887 --> 18:47.717
for anybody
who doesn't deserve it.

18:47.797 --> 18:49.467
♪

18:49.557 --> 18:51.267
That wouldn't make sense.

18:52.267 --> 18:53.597
Because...

18:54.517 --> 18:55.977
[grunts]

18:57.397 --> 18:59.267
[KIMIZUKA] This is my story!

19:03.777 --> 19:06.107
[birds chirping]

19:08.487 --> 19:11.487
[FUUBI] You're a bold man,
arresting a police officer.

19:12.537 --> 19:13.867
You really are.

19:13.947 --> 19:16.787
I still can't believe
you ate the seed, though.

19:17.117 --> 19:18.207
Yeah.

19:19.037 --> 19:21.297
It was a gift from the vampire.

19:21.377 --> 19:22.377
♪

19:22.457 --> 19:24.547
You know... you'll die.

19:26.757 --> 19:29.047
Well, I'll just deal with that
when it happens.

19:30.427 --> 19:33.557
I understand.
All right, you may as well go

19:33.637 --> 19:35.177
join the others then.

19:37.887 --> 19:39.147
Um, ma'am?

19:39.767 --> 19:41.067
-[NOCHES] Listen.
-Huh?

19:41.147 --> 19:42.267
I'm not the girl

19:42.357 --> 19:44.147
you seem to think
you're talking to.

19:44.227 --> 19:45.567
Got that, Charlotte?

19:45.647 --> 19:46.987
So, you're Noches?

19:47.067 --> 19:48.107
Thank goodness!

19:48.197 --> 19:49.197
[sighs]

19:49.697 --> 19:51.327
You always have to make
such a racket

19:51.407 --> 19:52.987
whenever you're around.

19:53.577 --> 19:57.037
Good grief, how am I supposed
to get a decent nap in?

19:57.117 --> 19:59.707
Noches, are you sure
you're not hurt?

20:01.287 --> 20:02.667
As far as I'm concerned,

20:02.747 --> 20:04.957
I've more than done my duty
at this point.

20:05.047 --> 20:07.257
You have? How so?

20:07.797 --> 20:09.007
Every single one of you

20:09.087 --> 20:10.677
had personal struggles
of your own

20:10.757 --> 20:12.427
that you needed to overcome.

20:13.057 --> 20:15.427
I am nothing more than a program
after all,

20:15.517 --> 20:17.517
created to help you
work through them.

20:17.597 --> 20:20.347
Nagisa Natsunagi
had to find out the truth

20:20.437 --> 20:22.107
about who she really was

20:22.187 --> 20:25.277
and learn how to come to terms
with everything in her past.

20:25.817 --> 20:27.527
Yui Saikawa had to come to terms

20:27.607 --> 20:29.487
with the events
of her parents' deaths

20:29.567 --> 20:32.487
and decide what she wanted to do
with the rest of her own life.

20:33.117 --> 20:36.997
Charlotte Arisaka Anderson
had to be freed from duty

20:37.077 --> 20:38.537
and develop a will of her own

20:38.617 --> 20:41.127
so she could decide
how she wanted to live her life.

20:41.627 --> 20:44.587
And finally,
Kimihiko Kimizuka...

20:45.297 --> 20:48.007
needed to learn to move on
from Siesta's death.

20:50.177 --> 20:52.467
My work here now
has come to an end,

20:52.887 --> 20:54.847
and Siesta is free to move on

20:54.927 --> 20:57.767
without harboring any regrets
to hold her back.

21:01.347 --> 21:03.807
-[KIMIZUKA] Is that really true?
-Uh?

21:03.897 --> 21:06.897
Even if we have all found a way
to put the past behind us

21:06.977 --> 21:08.647
and freed ourselves
from all the things

21:08.737 --> 21:10.567
that used
to keep us bound to it...

21:11.147 --> 21:13.527
Does that really mean
she had a happy ending?

21:14.527 --> 21:15.827
Kimihiko.

21:16.617 --> 21:19.657
[KIMIZUKA]
I can't forget she was crying,

21:19.747 --> 21:21.707
and she said
she didn't wanna die,

21:21.787 --> 21:24.167
-at least not like that.
-[gasps softly]

21:24.247 --> 21:26.207
[KIMIZUKA] If this was really
what she wanted

21:26.297 --> 21:27.957
and she had no regrets
at all about it,

21:28.047 --> 21:29.207
she wouldn't have let us see

21:29.297 --> 21:32.177
the tears running down her face
like that.

21:32.257 --> 21:33.587
Tell the truth,

21:33.677 --> 21:35.757
didn't you make that choice
by yourself,

21:35.847 --> 21:38.137
to allow us to see that scene
for ourselves?

21:38.217 --> 21:39.887
You wanted us
to set things right

21:39.967 --> 21:42.887
by undoing Siesta's choice
to sacrifice herself.

21:42.977 --> 21:43.897
I know that now.

21:43.977 --> 21:45.437
That's the real answer

21:45.517 --> 21:47.897
you wanted us to find
for ourselves all along.

21:48.477 --> 21:49.567
[gasps]

21:50.107 --> 21:51.147
♪

21:51.647 --> 21:52.647
[sighs]

21:54.157 --> 21:55.237
[gasps]

21:55.317 --> 21:58.237
Kimihiko, what are you doing?

21:58.327 --> 21:59.987
Listen here, Siesta.

22:00.077 --> 22:01.117
[NOCHES] Uh?

22:01.197 --> 22:03.827
I won't ever give up on you.

22:04.377 --> 22:07.667
Even if you are satisfied
with this as a conclusion,

22:08.047 --> 22:10.757
I'll never accept
your story ends this way.

22:11.257 --> 22:12.667
For all I know,

22:12.757 --> 22:14.887
nobody will ever understand
what I mean.

22:15.257 --> 22:18.557
Not Natsunagi,
nor Saikawa, nor Charlotte!

22:19.057 --> 22:20.807
And maybe bringing you back
would mean

22:20.887 --> 22:23.227
going against the very laws
of this world!

22:24.267 --> 22:26.437
But still, someday,

22:26.517 --> 22:30.647
I promise I'm gonna do it,
no matter what! I swear.

22:30.727 --> 22:32.607
I'll get you back!

22:36.277 --> 22:37.697
[Saikawa cries softly]

22:39.077 --> 22:41.157
You're an idiot, Kimizuka.

22:43.447 --> 22:45.917
Idiot, Kimizuka.

22:46.497 --> 22:48.167
[NATSUNAGI] You're an idiot...

22:49.297 --> 22:50.707
Kimizuka.

22:51.877 --> 22:53.127
[gasps]

22:54.547 --> 22:55.927
My goodness...

22:58.717 --> 23:01.177
Really, are you all stupid?

23:03.637 --> 23:04.767
[chuckles softly]

23:09.397 --> 23:11.477
[NOCHES] See that? The sun's up.

23:12.317 --> 23:14.987
Oh, yeah. This is a new start.

23:16.237 --> 23:19.197
So, you thought
the detective was already dead?

23:21.237 --> 23:22.617
Oh, no.

23:22.697 --> 23:25.867
This is only the start
of a long, long story

23:25.957 --> 23:27.207
still unfolding.

23:27.287 --> 23:28.997
About how I'll find a way

23:29.077 --> 23:31.667
to bring her back to me
for good.
